  "configuration_id": "config_033",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_004 (scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted, multiprofile) is the clear best at 0.713 acc, and ablations show transformer aggregation > avgpool (+3.5pp) and weighted fusion > concat (+2.5pp). scgpt is dramatically worse (0.494) and more expensive, so scvi_n200 is locked in. The single most impactful untested variable is the image encoder: all four completed runs use resnet50, while imagenet_vit_l (a larger, pretrained ViT) has not been tried. Question: does upgrading the image encoder to ViT-L while keeping the proven scvi_n200 + transformer + weighted + multiprofile stack push accuracy above 0.713? Why this is the best next experiment: it is a minimal, logical extension of the best configuration that tests the highest-leverage remaining design choice. Expected cost is moderate-to-high (~8–10 GPU hrs) due to ViT-L's larger parameter count versus ResNet-50, but well within the remaining budget and justified if it is the configuration most likely to yield the best final accuracy."
}

